From ba300163e661ace20382747d3c43b6b4ea911911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:11:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 51/77] feat: pin /pull to an exact Hugging Face revision

Port of the fork's B174 series (c9d7f27b6..4cc581600, 22 commits) onto the
refactored model manager (models/ingest, artifact_store, update_scan and the
route classes). POST /v1/pull accepts `revision` (a commit sha, branch or tag);
the main checkpoint repository is fetched at that commit into
snapshots/<sha>, refs/main is left alone, the pin is recorded per model in
.lemonade_registry.json (written atomically) and every later load resolves
inside the pinned snapshot. Pinned models are skipped by update checks; an
explicit /pull without revision releases the pin, other downloads restore it.
Collections, local imports, non-Hugging Face registries, self-managed
backends, offline mode and /models/register refuse revision with 400. Deleting
a model drops its pin. `lemonade pull --revision` passes it through.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
